  - Dione
  - Mimas
  internalStructure: 'Saturn has a hydrogen-helium envelope, a region of

    metallic
    hydrogen under high pressure and a deep interior

    containing heavier elements.'
  surfaceAndRings: 'Saturn has no conventional solid surface.

    Its spectacular
    ring system consists primarily of

    water-ice particles mixed with rocky
    material.

    The major ring groups include D, C, B, A, F, G and E.'
  magneticField: 'Saturn has a global magnetic field generated by

    electrically
    conducting material within its interior.

    Its magnetic field is unusually
    closely aligned

    with its rotational axis.'
